kiro-pixel-art
==============

This project is a port of the Claude Code plugin "pixel-plugin" to Kiro CLI.

Upstream project:
  willibrandon/pixel-plugin — https://github.com/willibrandon/pixel-plugin
  Copyright (c) 2025 Brandon Williams
  Licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE.upstream).

The following material is derived from the upstream project and remains under
its original MIT License:
  - The pixel art skills under skills/pixel-art-* (SKILL.md, reference.md,
    examples.md, and format references).
  - The command definitions adapted into skills/pixel-{new,setup,export,palette,help}.
  - The pixel-mcp server binary (NOT redistributed here; downloaded by the
    installer from the upstream repository at install time).

The following material is original to this port:
  - agents/pixel-art.json (Kiro agent configuration)
  - install/install.sh and install/uninstall.sh
  - Kiro-specific frontmatter and tool-name adaptations
  - README.md

Aseprite (https://www.aseprite.org/) is a separate product with its own
license and is not included or redistributed by this project.

The pixel-art-grid skill (skills/pixel-art-grid) is based on the dataset
"pixel-art-bench-lite" by AINovice2005
(https://huggingface.co/datasets/AINovice2005/pixel-art-bench-lite),
licensed under Apache-2.0. Only the task format and the seven subject prompts
are reused; no dataset images are redistributed.

The pixel-art-rules skill (skills/pixel-art-rules) is an original rulebook whose
rules are synthesised and paraphrased (no text copied) from established pixel-art
teaching. Credit to those sources:
  - Pixeli — Pixel Art Knowledge Base (https://pixeli.pebbly.space/knowledge),
    MIT-licensed plugin/site by pebbly.
  - Pixel Logic by Michael Azzi.
  - Pedro Medeiros / Saint11 (https://saint11.art/blog/pixel-art-tutorials/).
  - Daniel Silber — Pixel Art for Game Developers.
  - SLYNYRD / Pixelblog (https://www.slynyrd.com/pixelblog-catalogue).
  - Lospec Pixel Art Tutorials (https://lospec.com/pixel-art-tutorials).
  - Derek Yu (https://www.derekyu.com/extras.html).
  - Pixel Joint — The Pixel Art Tutorial.
  - Helm — Pixelation tutorials.
These sources are referenced for study; no copyrighted text or images from them
are redistributed in this repository.

examples/starry-night-vangogh.* is an original pixel-art homage to Vincent van
Gogh's "The Starry Night" (1889), which is in the public domain. No copyrighted
reproduction is redistributed; the pixels were drawn programmatically.
